[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/cslib/pull/799\">cslib#799</a> this definition is added:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Preserves</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">⦄,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Are we missing a standard Mathlib way to write this? This is defeq with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsUpperSet#doc\">docs#IsUpperSet</a>, but this would be an awkward defeq abuse, right?</p>",
        "id": 616534088,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786711303
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>IsUpperSet</code> requires <code>[LE α]</code>, which is not the case here.</p>",
        "id": 616589439,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786727399
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I mean this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Preserves</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">⦄,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Preserves</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">IsUpperSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616593366,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786728652
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>(letI : LE α := ⟨r⟩; IsUpperSet (.ofPred P))</code> avoids the defeq abuse</p>",
        "id": 616594283,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786728901
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But indeed the local instance is not a good approach</p>",
        "id": 616594330,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786728912
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>r ≤ (Implies on P)</code> is another cursed way to spell it</p>",
        "id": 616594741,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786729017
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Though that spelling does rather nicely give you monotonicity in <code>r</code> for free</p>",
        "id": 616594934,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786729070
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would guess the right approach here is to redefine <code>IsUpperSet</code> as <code>IsRelSet LE.le</code> or similar</p>",
        "id": 616595037,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786729102
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Generally I'd claim it's not worth having both set and predicate spellings of the same idea</p>",
        "id": 616595150,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786729133
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, I agree in principle, but I'm really not sure overall. It seems confusing to use <code>LE</code> because often the relation is some reduction we use notation for, and there are theorems about how different reductions interact.</p>",
        "id": 616598466,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786730013
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't follow; my claim is that in mathlib, we should generalize away from LE, and then recover the existing definition in mathlib as a special case</p>",
        "id": 616605479,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786732197
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/513188-CSLib/topic/relations.20that.20preserve.20a.20predicate/near/616595037\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would guess the right approach here is to redefine <code>IsUpperSet</code> as <code>IsRelSet LE.le</code> or similar</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes please! This has been discussed in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36626\">#36626</a> and <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Difference.20between.20.60IsAntichain.60.20and.20.60IsUpperSet.60/near/614188212\">#mathlib4 &gt; Difference between &#96;IsAntichain&#96; and &#96;IsUpperSet&#96; @ 💬</a></p>\n<p>wdyt about <code>Set.IsRelClosed</code>? Or maybe we should have upper &amp; lower versions (differ by <code>flip</code>)</p>",
        "id": 616605567,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786732218
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/513188-CSLib/topic/relations.20that.20preserve.20a.20predicate/near/616605479\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't follow; my claim is that in mathlib, we should generalize away from LE, and then recover the existing definition in mathlib as a special case</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>We're on the same page, I just meant given what's currently in Mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 616606355,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786732495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can't find <code>IsRelSet</code> in mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 616627099,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786740277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is a potential name for the Mathlib refactor being discussed above, not something existing.</p>",
        "id": 616627212,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786740320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see.  Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 616627387,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786740390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess we can go ahead with <code>Preserves</code> for now then?</p>",
        "id": 616887128,
        "sender_full_name": "Fabrizio Montesi",
        "timestamp": 1786949844
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think so, and if Mathlib adds a <code>Set.IsRelClosed</code> in the future we can switch to this.</p>",
        "id": 616887856,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786950086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Agreed</p>",
